# Operating System Security

## Hardware
- Physical components (CPU, RAM, keyboard, screen, storage devices)

## OS Role
- Acts as a bridge between hardware and software

## Application
- Cannot directly use hardware
- Uses OS to interact with hardware

---

# Examples of Operating Systems
- Desktop: Windows
- Mobile: Android, iOS
- Server: Linux, Windows Server

---

# Why OS Security is Important
- Devices store sensitive data:
  - Private chats, photos
  - Emails
  - Passwords
  - Banking apps
- Unauthorized access can lead to:
  - Data theft
  - Misuse

---

# CIA Triad

## Confidentiality
- Only authorized users can access data

## Integrity
- Data should not be altered

## Availability
- System should be accessible when needed

---

# Common OS Security Threats
- Weak passwords
- Weak file permissions
- Malicious programs (malware)

---

# Important Commands

## Current User
- Command: whoami
- Shows current user

## Remote Login
- Command: ssh <username>@<ip>
- Used for remote access

## List Files
- Command: ls
- Displays files in directory

---

# Extra Commands

## View File Content
- Command: cat <filename>
- Displays file content

## Command History
- Command: history
- Shows previously used commands
